From: Sreesai Arjun <sreesaiarjun@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AP_OSD: wait for the AT7456E NVM read before reading CMDO

AP_OSD_MAX7456::check_font_char() sends one full-duplex burst:
VM0=0 (OSD off), CMAH=chr, CMM=0x50 (read NVM character into shadow
RAM), then 54 x (CMAL=x, CMDO read).  The first CMDO data byte is
clocked 4 bytes after the CMM write: 3.2 us at the 10 MHz SCLK most
boards use (6.4 us at the 5 MHz this board runs SPI2 at).

That is enough for the MAX7456 (NVM read 0.5 us), but not for the
AT7456E clone fitted to most current boards.  AT7456E-S402-V1.1:
  - p.36 command execution table: CMM = 0x50 read completes (STAT[5]
    clears) after 22 us min / 30 us typ; note 3 under the table: when
    fixed delays are used, design to the typical value.
  - same table: VM0[3] = 0 (display off) takes 0..18 us min / 30 us
    typ; p.29 (CMM register): NVM read/write commands issued while the
    display is enabled or STAT[5] is busy are ignored.  The p.34 read
    procedure has an explicit 30 us wait after VM0[3] = 0.

With the single burst the CMDO bytes come from stale shadow RAM, every
character compares unequal and update_font() rewrites all 256
characters (>= 256 x 15 ms) at every boot and on every font change,
consuming NVM write endurance.  On a runtime font change (display on)
the CMM read can additionally be ignored outright.

Split the burst into three transfers on the same buffer (so the rx
byte offsets parsed below are unchanged) with a 40 us wait after the
OSD-disable and after CMM = 0x50 (typ 30 us + 33 % margin; ChibiOS
delay_microseconds() rounds up to whole ticks so the wait is a
minimum).  Both are overridable from hwdef.  Cost on a MAX7456: 256 x
~80 us = ~20 ms extra at boot only.

The timing analysis is from the datasheet and the Nano H743 AIO repo
(analysis/osd_vtx_bec_analysis.py, firmware/osd_at7456e simulator);
not yet confirmed on hardware.

---
--- a/libraries/AP_OSD/AP_OSD_MAX7456.cpp
+++ b/libraries/AP_OSD/AP_OSD_MAX7456.cpp
@@ -122,6 +122,19 @@
 //time to wait nvm flash complete
 #define MAX_NVM_WAIT 10000
 
+// NVM -> shadow RAM read (CMM = READ_NVR) completion time. MAX7456: 0.5 us.
+// AT7456E (AT7456E-S402-V1.1 p.36 table): 22 us min, 30 us typ, and note 3
+// there says fixed delays must be designed to the typical value. Clearing
+// VM0[3] (OSD display off) likewise takes up to 30 us (same table) and a
+// CMM command issued while STAT[5] is busy is ignored (p.31, CMM register).
+// Both waits are therefore inserted between separate SPI transfers.
+#ifndef MAX7456_NVM_READ_DELAY_US
+#define MAX7456_NVM_READ_DELAY_US 40
+#endif
+#ifndef MAX7456_OSD_DISABLE_DELAY_US
+#define MAX7456_OSD_DISABLE_DELAY_US 40
+#endif
+
 //black and white level
 #ifndef WHITEBRIGHTNESS
 #define WHITEBRIGHTNESS 0x01
@@ -201,8 +214,15 @@
         buffer_add_cmd(MAX7456ADD_CMAL, x);
         buffer_add_cmd(MAX7456ADD_CMDO, 0xFF);
     }
+    // buffer layout: [0..1] VM0=0, [2..5] CMAH=chr + CMM=READ_NVR,
+    // [6..] CMAL/CMDO pairs. Send it as three transfers so the OSD-disable
+    // and the NVM read have completed before the next command (AT7456E).
     _dev->get_semaphore()->take_blocking();
-    _dev->transfer_fullduplex(buffer, buffer_offset);
+    _dev->transfer_fullduplex(buffer, 2);
+    hal.scheduler->delay_microseconds(MAX7456_OSD_DISABLE_DELAY_US);
+    _dev->transfer_fullduplex(&buffer[2], 4);
+    hal.scheduler->delay_microseconds(MAX7456_NVM_READ_DELAY_US);
+    _dev->transfer_fullduplex(&buffer[6], buffer_offset - 6);
     _dev->get_semaphore()->give();
 
     //skip response from MAX7456ADD_VM0/MAX7456ADD_CMAH...
